====================================================================
PolyKernel T29 Wave 6: HAPPY evidence - Modal CUDA-toolkit Image +
  app skeleton (CURRENT modal API). The image DEFINITION + the App
  construct locally with NO Modal token and NO Docker (constructing
  a modal.Image / modal.App is pure). Materialising the image (running
  its layers, compiling the engine) happens only on deploy/serve, which
  is the owner-gated cloud step (Todo 33) behind a MODAL_TOKEN.
  modal installed via devenv.nix (python3Packages.modal); the dev shell
  has no pip, so nix withPackages is the install path.
====================================================================

### [1] modal installed via devenv.nix; import modal.image + version ###
$ python3 -c "import modal; import modal.image; print(\"modal\", modal.__version__)"
modal 1.5.2

devenv.nix python package set (modal added; numpy/ml-dtypes/pytest retained):
  python = pkgs.python3.withPackages (ps: with ps; [
    numpy
    ml-dtypes
    pytest
    modal
  ]);

### [2] regression: numpy / ml_dtypes / pytest still import (env not broken) ###
$ python3 -c "import numpy, ml_dtypes, pytest; ..."
numpy 2.5.0 | ml_dtypes 0.5.4 | pytest 9.0.3
python: Python 3.14.6

### [3] modal 1.5.2 API methods used by modal/image.py are CURRENT (introspection) ###
Image.from_registry(tag: str, secret: modal.secret._Secret | None = None, *, setup_dockerfile_commands: list[str] = [], force_build: bool = False, add_python: str | None = None, **kwargs) -> '_Image'
Image.entrypoint(self, entrypoint_commands: list[str]) -> '_Image'
Image.apt_install(self, *packages: str | list[str], force_build: bool = False, env: dict[str, str | None] | None = None, secrets: collections.abc.Collection[modal.secret._Secret] | None = None, gpu: str | None = None) -> '_Image'
Image.add_local_dir(self, local_path: str | pathlib.Path, remote_path: str, *, copy: bool = False, ignore: collections.abc.Sequence[str] | collections.abc.Callable[[pathlib.Path], bool] = []) -> '_Image'
Image.run_commands(self, *commands: str | list[str], env: dict[str, str | None] | None = None, secrets: collections.abc.Collection[modal.secret._Secret] | None = None, volumes: dict[str | pathlib.PurePosixPath, modal.volume._Volume] | None = None, gpu: str | None = None, force_build: bool = False) -> '_Image'
App.__init__(self, name: str | None = None, *, tags: dict[str, str] | None = None, image: modal._image._Image | None = None, secrets: collections.abc.Sequence[modal.secret._Secret] = [], volumes: dict[str | pathlib.PurePosixPath, modal.volume._Volume] = {}, include_source: bool = True) -> None
=> from_registry(add_python=...), entrypoint(list), apt_install(*pkgs),
   add_local_dir(local, remote_path, copy=...), run_commands(*cmds),
   App(name, image=...) all present + current in modal 1.5.2.
   (add_local_dir docstring: it REPLACES the deprecated copy_local_dir -
    add_local_dir itself is current, NOT deprecated.)

### [4] modal/image.py constructs the engine Image (NO token, NO Docker) ###
$ python3 modal/image.py   (executes the module; builds the Image object)
exit 0 (image.py executed; image object built)
image type        : modal.image.Image
isinstance Image  : True
base registry tag : nvidia/cuda:12.8.1-devel-ubuntu24.04
add_python        : 3.12 (REQUIRED: NVIDIA images ship no Python)
remote app dir    : /app

### [5] modal/app.py constructs modal.App("polykernel", image=...) (NO token) ###
$ python3 modal/app.py   (loads sibling image.py via importlib - the modal/
                          dir name collides with the modal SDK package, so the
                          sibling is loaded by path, not via modal.image)
exit 0 (app.py executed; App object built)
app type          : modal.app.App
isinstance App    : True
app.name          : polykernel
app.image type    : Image (the engine image is wired in)

### [6] modal deploy LOADS the definition, then blocks on the absent token ###
    (proves the image/app spec is valid; deploy is SKIPPED - no token, no spend)
$ echo "MODAL_TOKEN=[${MODAL_TOKEN:-<unset>}]"
MODAL_TOKEN=[<unset>]
$ timeout 45 modal deploy modal/app.py
╭─ Error ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Token missing. Could not authenticate client. If you have token credentials, │
│ see modal.com/docs/sdk/py/latest/modal.config for setup help. If you are a   │
│ new user, register an account at modal.com, then run `modal token new`.      │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
deploy exit: 1 (1 = auth failure; the CLI parsed app.py + built the
             App+Image, then failed ONLY on authentication - no definition error).

### [7] modal client version PINNED (avoid API drift) ###
$ cat modal/requirements.txt
# PolyKernel Modal deployment client - PINNED to avoid API drift (Todo 29 / Wave 6).
#
# modal/image.py + modal/app.py are written against this exact version's API
# (verified by introspection): Image.from_registry(..., add_python=...),
# .entrypoint(list), .apt_install(*pkgs), .add_local_dir(local, remote_path,
# copy=...), .run_commands(*cmds), and modal.App(name, image=...).
#
# In the nix dev shell modal is provided by devenv.nix (python3Packages.modal),
# NOT pip (the shell has no pip). This pin documents the version the definitions
# target so a non-nix environment reproduces the same API.
modal==1.5.2

### [8] DEPLOY SKIPPED (no MODAL_TOKEN) - opt-in cloud path ###
Cloud deploy is opt-in behind a token that is ABSENT here (no spend). To deploy:
    modal setup                  # one-time auth (register + modal token new)
    modal deploy modal/app.py    # builds the CUDA image (compiles the engine
                                 #   at image-build time) + deploys the app
The GPU endpoints (/predict /benchmark /kernels /report) attach to this app in
Todo 30; cold-start Todo 31; kernel cache Todo 32; owner-gated deploy Todo 33.
